From: Chua Zheng Leong <melynx@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] desktop/layer: recheck idle inhibitors on layer map and unmap

CInputManager::newIdleInhibitor() evaluates a layer-surface inhibitor's
visibility exactly once, when the zwp_idle_inhibitor_v1 arrives. A client
that creates the inhibitor for a freshly created layer window sends it
before the surface's first buffer commit, so aliveAndVisible() is false
and the compositor records "not inhibiting". The only other callers of
recheckIdleInhibitorStatus() are toplevel map/unmap in Window.cpp; a
layer surface mapping later never triggers a re-evaluation, so the
inhibitor stays dead until some unrelated toplevel opens or closes.

Quickshell's IdleInhibitor hits this on every output hotplug: its window
is rebuilt, the inhibitor is re-created before the new surface maps, and
the idle timeouts fire with the toggle still reporting active.

Re-evaluate on layer map and on both unmap paths.
---
 src/desktop/view/LayerSurface.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/src/desktop/view/LayerSurface.cpp
+++ b/src/desktop/view/LayerSurface.cpp
@@ -170,6 +170,10 @@
 
     m_layerSurface->m_surface->map();
 
+    // an idle inhibitor created for this surface before it mapped was scored
+    // as not visible; re-evaluate now that it is
+    g_pInputManager->recheckIdleInhibitorStatus();
+
     // fix if it changed its mon
     const auto PMONITOR = m_monitor.lock();
 
@@ -236,6 +240,8 @@
         if (m_layerSurface && m_layerSurface->m_surface)
             m_layerSurface->m_surface->unmap();
 
+        g_pInputManager->recheckIdleInhibitorStatus();
+
         return;
     }
 
@@ -258,6 +264,8 @@
     if (m_layerSurface && m_layerSurface->m_surface)
         m_layerSurface->m_surface->unmap();
 
+    g_pInputManager->recheckIdleInhibitorStatus();
+
     const auto PMONITOR = m_monitor.lock();
 
     const bool WASLASTFOCUS = g_pSeatManager->m_state.keyboardFocus == m_wlSurface->resource() || g_pSeatManager->m_state.pointerFocus == m_wlSurface->resource();
